Subject: [PATCH] webgpu: make the offline shader harness match the engine

The GPU-free harness (glsl2spv -> the driver's 11 preprocess passes -> Tint) is
how every shader-translation defect in this series was found and verified. It
was not reproducing the engine.

1. Wrong target environment. glsl2spv hardcoded EShTargetVulkan_1_0 /
   EShTargetSpv_1_0, but RenderingShaderContainerWebGPU reports
   SHADER_LANGUAGE_VULKAN_VERSION_1_1 + SHADER_SPIRV_VERSION_1_3, and
   modules/glslang/register_types.cpp feeds those straight into glslang. So the
   harness compiled every shader against a SPIR-V version the runtime never
   uses. That is not cosmetic: SPIR-V 1.0 emits SSBOs as StorageClass::Uniform +
   BufferBlock rather than StorageClass::StorageBuffer, and any shader using
   subgroup ops cannot be compiled at all.

   That last part actively hid a bug. cluster_render.glsl failed at the
   GLSL->SPIR-V step, so it never reached Tint, so the TINT_UNIMPLEMENTED abort
   on gl_HelperInvocation (fixed in 0015) was invisible. Now defaults to the
   engine's 1.1/1.3; GLSL2SPV_SPV=10 restores the old target for bisecting.

2. One crashing module reported as "everything is broken". Tint aborts take down
   the whole `--batch` process, and convert_spirv_batch turned a non-zero exit
   into `return {}`, marking every module in the batch as a Tint failure. A
   single bad shader read as 183 failures and 0 successes. It now degrades to
   per-file conversion so the crasher is isolated and named and the rest still
   convert.

3. Silent failure lists. Tint failures were counted but never named, so the
   summary said "5 tint failures" without saying which five. They are now
   printed.

4. cluster_render variants. The harness only knew the single "default" variant;
   it now mirrors the four variants cluster_builder_rd.cpp actually builds, so
   both the subgroup and non-subgroup paths are exercised.

Also adds two tools:

  - tint_cli/build_glsl2spv.sh: builds glsl2spv from Godot's vendored glslang
    alone (~1 minute) instead of requiring the full Tint + SPIRV-Tools build
    (~30). Source list and defines mirror modules/glslang/SCsub. Statically
    links the toolchain runtime, without which a MinGW-built binary dies with
    0xC0000139 (STATUS_ENTRYPOINT_NOT_FOUND) the moment Python or PowerShell
    launches it.
  - tint_cli/probe_one.py: runs one shader variant through Tint on its own and
    prints the raw error and the SPIR-V version header, which is what made the
    HelperInvocation abort identifiable rather than just a count.

Sweep at the corrected target env, with 0015 applied: 182 modules compiled,
6 Tint failures -- tonemap_mobile subpass x2 (Forward Mobile only; WebGPU has no
subpasses), screen_space_reflection_filter (storage-texture format inference,
the one real Forward+ gap), cluster_render subgroup variants x2 (not selected on
WebGPU), and sdfgi_debug_probes (editor debug visualisation).

diff --git a/drivers/webgpu/tint_cli/glsl2spv.cpp b/drivers/webgpu/tint_cli/glsl2spv.cpp
--- a/drivers/webgpu/tint_cli/glsl2spv.cpp
+++ b/drivers/webgpu/tint_cli/glsl2spv.cpp
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 //   glsl2spv <vert|frag|comp> <in.glsl> <out.spv>
 //   tint_convert_cli <out.spv>            # hang == the runtime bug, no GPU needed
 #include <cstdio>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <fstream>
 #include <sstream>
 #include <string>
@@ -69,8 +70,24 @@
 	glslang::TShader shader(stage);
 	shader.setStrings(srcs, 1);
 	shader.setEnvInput(glslang::EShSourceGlsl, stage, glslang::EShClientVulkan, 100);
-	shader.setEnvClient(glslang::EShClientVulkan, glslang::EShTargetVulkan_1_0);
-	shader.setEnvTarget(glslang::EShTargetSpv, glslang::EShTargetSpv_1_0);
+
+	// Match the engine, not an arbitrary default. RenderingShaderContainerWebGPU
+	// reports SHADER_LANGUAGE_VULKAN_VERSION_1_1 + SHADER_SPIRV_VERSION_1_3, and
+	// the runtime feeds those straight into glslang (modules/glslang/register_types.cpp).
+	// Targeting 1.0 here silently diverges from the engine: SPIR-V 1.0 emits SSBOs as
+	// StorageClass::Uniform + BufferBlock, and shaders using subgroup ops (the Forward+
+	// cluster builder) fail to compile at all, so they never even reach Tint.
+	// Override with GLSL2SPV_SPV=10|13 only to bisect a version-specific problem.
+	glslang::EShTargetClientVersion client_ver = glslang::EShTargetVulkan_1_1;
+	glslang::EShTargetLanguageVersion spv_ver = glslang::EShTargetSpv_1_3;
+	if (const char *e = getenv("GLSL2SPV_SPV")) {
+		if (std::string(e) == "10") {
+			client_ver = glslang::EShTargetVulkan_1_0;
+			spv_ver = glslang::EShTargetSpv_1_0;
+		}
+	}
+	shader.setEnvClient(glslang::EShClientVulkan, client_ver);
+	shader.setEnvTarget(glslang::EShTargetSpv, spv_ver);
 
 	if (!shader.parse(GetDefaultResources(), 450, false, EShMsgDefault)) {
 		fprintf(stderr, "GLSL parse error:\n%s\n%s\n", shader.getInfoLog(), shader.getInfoDebugLog());
